  "description": "T1 item 9 (testbenches shipped), both partitions, 256 x 32 reference instance. Analog: both bench families - column (bit-slice) benches sim/column (read access, write completion, in-situ SNM, with Monte Carlo and negative controls) and isolated-bitcell benches sim/bitcell (read/hold SNM, write trip, with Monte Carlo and negative controls), whose record makers publish the cell-level figures under sim/bitcell/records/. Digital: cocotb bench rtl/tb/cocotb against the RTL, the synthesized netlist and seeded faults, plus the Icarus smoke benches. sim/bitcell/corners/ and sim/bitcell/records/ hold measurement results, not harness: the records are append-only, so listing them would force a fresh item-9 re-attestation on every new measurement without adding any drift detection. cold_start runs one local single-corner probe of the column benches and the whole digital bench (the bitcell and Monte Carlo grids run as the committed klt sim requests on the batch fleet, not locally; see sim/column/README.md and sim/bitcell/README.md).",
